  <data key="d36">Escalating export controls and intrusive extraterritorial regulations tied to the US–China tech rivalry produce diplomatic friction and reciprocal policy measures among third‑party states, degrading the political trust and routine channels that underpin cross‑border security and intelligence cooperation related to the Russia–Ukraine theater.</data>
