<edge source="populist_election_wave::leading_vote_share" target="global_bond_stress::sovereign_spread" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A rising vote share for a populist front‑runner conveys a higher probability of aggressive fiscal measures or contract repudiation, prompting investors to reprice sovereign credit risk and bid up spreads as the election outcome becomes more likely to affect debt-servicing policies.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">populist_election_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="populist_election_wave::leading_vote_share" target="middle_east_war::maritime_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A high leading vote share for a populist candidate provides a perceived domestic mandate that enables more assertive regional postures and increased material and political support for proxy actors or naval patrols, raising the frequency of hostile incidents against commercial shipping in the Middle East.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">populist_election_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="populist_election_wave::leading_vote_share" target="russia_ukraine_war::transnational_coop_cap" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A strong populist leading vote share provides a political mandate to an incoming government to scale back alliance commitments, restrict intelligence-sharing and limit joint deployments, directly weakening cross‑border security cooperation capacity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">populist_election_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="populist_election_wave::leading_vote_share" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_activity_inte" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A larger leading vote share for a populist candidate strengthens their mandate to pursue tech-sovereignty and security agendas, prompting faster and more assertive regulatory interventions (export controls, investment screens, procurement rules) affecting large-scale AI deployment.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">populist_election_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
