<edge source="populist_election_wave::policy_uncertainty" target="global_bond_stress::sovereign_spread" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in perceived policy uncertainty raises the sovereign risk premium as investors demand compensation for greater fiscal/regulatory unpredictability and shorter horizon for policy commitments, pushing up sovereign spreads within weeks as secondary markets reprice exposure.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">populist_election_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="populist_election_wave::policy_uncertainty" target="middle_east_war::freight_rate_index" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising policy uncertainty linked to a populist election spike increases perceived geopolitical and operational risk for shippers and insurers, which raises insurance premiums and charter risk premia and thereby pushes up freight rates on routes through the region.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">populist_election_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">middle_east_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="populist_election_wave::policy_uncertainty" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_conflict_lvl" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Elevated policy uncertainty in key supporter states creates ambiguity about deterrence and response plans that adversaries (e.g., Russian commanders) can exploit, prompting opportunistic increases in kinetic operations to test resolve.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">populist_election_wave</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="populist_election_wave::policy_uncertainty" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::capital_flow_to_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising election-driven policy uncertainty raises risk premia and delays board-level approvals and VC commitments, causing investors and corporates to pull back or defer new financing for AI compute and model projects.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">populist_election_wave</data>
